{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Oklahoma Army National Guard is the Army National Guard component of the Oklahoma National Guard.","title":"Oklahoma Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The Commander in Chief of the Oklahoma National Guard is the Governor of Oklahoma, who appoints the State Adjutant General (TAG), a Major General from either Army or Air.","title":"Oklahoma Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Currently, the TAG is Major General (MG) Robbie L. Asher.","title":"Oklahoma Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The previous TAG was Myles Deering MG Deering retired and was appointed Director of Veterans Affairs for the State of Oklahoma.","title":"Oklahoma Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 189th Field Artillery Regiment, today consists of 1st Battalion, 189th Field Artillery Regiment, and 2nd Battalion (General Services) Field Artillery Regiment which are headquartered in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma.","title":"189th Field Artillery Regiment (United States)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was a part of the 45th Infantry Division, Oklahoma Army National Guard.","title":"189th Field Artillery Regiment (United States)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The Regiment only retains its affiliation with the Field Artillery branch for purposes of history and lineage and is the core cadre and leadership of the Oklahoma Regional Training Institute (OKRTI).","title":"189th Field Artillery Regiment (United States)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Its parent unit is the Joint Force Headquarters of the Oklahoma Army National Guard.","title":"189th Field Artillery Regiment (United States)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 28th Infantry Division ("Keystone") is a unit of the Army National Guard and is the oldest division-sized unit in the armed forces of the United States.","title":"28th Infantry Division (United States)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Some of the units of the division can trace their lineage to Benjamin Franklin's battalion, "The Pennsylvania Associators" (1747-1777).","title":"28th Infantry Division (United States)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The division was officially established in 1879 and was later redesignated as the 28th Division in 1917, after the entry of America into the First World War.","title":"28th Infantry Division (United States)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It is today part of the Pennsylvania Army National Guard, Maryland Army National Guard, Ohio Army National Guard, and New Jersey Army National Guard.","title":"28th Infantry Division (United States)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Oklahoma Air National Guard (OK ANG) is the air force militia of the State of Oklahoma, United States of America.","title":"Oklahoma Air National Guard"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is, along with the Oklahoma Army National Guard, an element of the Oklahoma National Guard.","title":"Oklahoma Air National Guard"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Illinois Army National Guard is a component of the United States Army and the United States National Guard.","title":"Illinois Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" With the Illinois Air National Guard it is part of the Illinois National Guard.","title":"Illinois Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" National coordination of various state National Guard units are maintained through the National Guard Bureau.","title":"Illinois Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The Illinois Army National Guard is composed of approximately 10,000 soldiers.","title":"Illinois Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Ohio Army National Guard is a part of the Ohio National Guard and the Army National Guard of the United States Army.","title":"Ohio Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is also a component of the organized militia of the state of Ohio, which also includes the Ohio Naval Militia, the Ohio Military Reserve and the Ohio Air National Guard.","title":"Ohio Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The Ohio Army National Guard consists of a variety of combat, combat support and combat service support units.","title":"Ohio Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" As of September 2010, its end strength exceeded 11,400 soldiers.","title":"Ohio Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Its headquarters is the Beightler Armory in Columbus, Ohio.","title":"Ohio Army National Guard"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Many units conduct Annual Training at Camp Grayling, Michigan.","title":"Ohio Army National Guard"}],"peer_messages":["Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Oklahoma Army National Guard is the Army National Guard component of the Oklahoma National Guard.","title":"Oklahoma Army National Guard"}
